                    <occupation>Poet</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See Ed Pope: 2.7.1789 Stirling at Billingsgate with Robinson and c. /
                            Sterling at Holcroft's 13.7.1794. In Godwin's 1796 list for 1789 and in
                            1794 version. Joseph Sterling DNB fl 1765-1794. Sterling's poems were
                            published in Dublin in 1781 by Luke White, in London in 1794 by T Payne,
                            and in London in 1789 by Robinson, so three of his publishers were
                            present at this dinner. He lived chiefly in Ireland but his presence in
                            London in 1794 coincided with the publication of his Odes there. George
                            Cecil of Dublin was his uncle, published his first work and left him a
                            legacy.</p>
                    </note>
